Nothing much to say about these:
* colour_overlay.dds
* lf_sea_colour.dds
* snow_mask.dds

==== shroud_heights.dds ====
Terry has a "Fill from terrain" for the shroud height layer, just click that and process. Good enough.

==== corruption mask.dds ====
White = Corruption shows at 1%
Black = Corruption shows at 100%
There doesn't seem to be a way to automatically generate this using Terry or BOB. So hand-painting it is (or clever python scripts!).
For each regions, you want white around settlements, then greys slowly getting darker until the borders are reached.

